/target
# Mirrored off the Pi by deploy/sync-sysroot.sh; ~300 MB and host-specific.
/sysroot
# Target-architecture .debs fetched by deploy/fetch-target-debs.sh. Tens of MB, and
# re-downloadable from the Debian archive at any time.
/deploy/debs
# M0 hardware survey output, per the command in the README. Describes one particular Pi
# (its panel modes, DRM layout, touch device, idle load), so it is a local observation
# rather than something the repo should assert about anyone else's hardware.
/m0-survey.txt
*.ppm
# Rendered frames from --offscreen runs, which land wherever --out points.
*.png
# ...except the panel screenshots in the README, which are checked in deliberately. They are
# regenerated by the commands in the "Regenerating the screenshots" section, so they can be
# refreshed whenever the UI changes rather than drifting silently.
!/docs/images/*.png
# Archive trust anchors cached by deploy/fetch-target-debs.sh. The verifiable thing is the
# pinned fingerprint in that script, which IS version-controlled; this is just a cache.
/deploy/keyrings
# Sessions pulled off the Pi by deploy/capture.sh. Real recordings from real trips —
# large, and specific to one flight, so kept out of the repo but NOT out of the way.
/captures

# Snapshots fetched by tools/mock-stratux/fetch-snapshot.sh. They carry ODbL traffic data
# from adsb.lol, which is a different licence from this repo, and they are re-fetchable in
# seconds. See docs/free-aviation-data.md.
snapshot*.json
